Feature: scriptor
  Find and select repository scripts with an interactive terminal.

  @version
  Scenario: Print the build version
    When I run "scriptor --version"
    Then exit code is 0
    Then output contains "0.1.0+unknown"

  @failure
  Scenario: Reject extra options
    When I run "scriptor --list" expecting exit code 1
    Then exit code is 1
    Then output contains "usage: scriptor [--version]"

  @failure
  Scenario: Report an empty scan
    When I run "scriptor" expecting exit code 1
    Then exit code is 1
    Then output contains "no scripts found"

  @interactive @git
  Scenario: Filter and run from the repository root with inherited input
    When I run "scriptor-terminal run"
    Then exit code is 0
    Then output contains "answer=hello"
    Then file "repo/ran.txt" exists

  @interactive @cancel
  Scenario: Cancel without running a sole result
    When I run "scriptor-terminal cancel"
    Then exit code is 0
    Then file "repo/ran.txt" does not exist

  @interactive @failure
  Scenario: Preserve the selected script exit code
    When I run "scriptor-terminal fail" expecting exit code 7
    Then exit code is 7
    Then output contains "Running scripts/build task.sh"

  @interactive @failure
  Scenario: Require a terminal when scripts exist
    When I run "scriptor-terminal nonterminal" expecting exit code 1
    Then exit code is 1
    Then output contains "requires an interactive terminal"
